; DIMLINEAR with typed points: the direction follows where the dimension line
; location is with respect to the rectangle of the two origins (PT26, #713):
; above and below give a horizontal dimension, right and left a vertical one.
; Prompts from autocad-quote.txt (dxf-test-file 1ad04b0), in English.
; Values by hand from PT23 with ISO-25: line-point is the foot of the second
; origin, as AutoCAD writes group 10 (autocad-quote.dxf, handles 93 and A1);
; text-point is the text centre, DIMGAP + DIMTXT/2 = 1.875 above the line.
; Every dimension has six graphics records (three lines, two arrows, the
; text): the editor numbers them after the dimension, as AutoCAD does.
DIMLINEAR
0,0
40,30
20,40
DIMLINEAR
0,0
40,30
20,-10
DIMLINEAR
0,0
40,30
50,15
DIMLINEAR
0,0
40,30
-10,15
